      "symbol": "Utopia\\Database\\Adapter\\Postgres::createDocument",
      "description": "A bound string that is not valid UTF-8 (up to its first NUL) makes PDO's execute() return false without running the statement and without an error (PQescapeStringConn fails, PHP 8.5's pgsql quoter returns NULL): createDocument() reports success for a document it never inserted; a NUL byte cuts every bound string ('a\\0b' is stored as 'a')",
      "case": "Adapter-Documents.json#strings, unicode, quotes and bytes"
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Database\\Adapter\\Postgres::createDocument",
      "description": "Permission roles are written into the permissions INSERT as raw SQL literals ('{$permission}', only double quotes removed): a role with a single quote is a syntax error after the document row was inserted",
      "case": "Adapter-Documents.json#strings, unicode, quotes and bytes"
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Database\\Adapter::setMetadata",
      "description": "Metadata is written into a /* key: value */ comment unescaped: a value containing */ breaks every later statement of the adapter, and resetMetadata() keeps the transform",
      "case": "Adapter-Settings.json#metadata and transforms"
    },
